{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/960954-ghost-in-the-shell-with-cofd","id":960954,"title":"Ghost in the Shell with CofD?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-31T02:55:07-07:00","id":960954,"title":"Ghost in the Shell with CofD?","content":"Has anybody done a conversion of GITS with the CofD/nWOD rules?<br /> <br /> I believe the ruleset is a good fit if you hack it enough (pun intended)<br /> <br /> Here's what I came up with<br /> <br /> SKILLS:<br /> <br /> Mental:<br /> <br /> Academics<br /> Investigation<br /> Medicine<br /> Science<br /> Politics<br /> Craft<br /> Hacking (an &quot;attack/defense&quot; skill)<br /> Programming (a &quot;create&quot; skill)<br /> <br /> <br /> Physical:<br /> <br /> Athletics<br /> Brawl<br /> Weapons<br /> Firearms<br /> Larceny<br /> Stealth<br /> Survival<br /> Drive<br /> <br /> Social:<br /> <br /> Empathy<br /> Expression<br /> Persuasion<br /> Socialize<br /> Intimidation<br /> Subterfuge<br /> Streetwise<br /> AI Ken (knowledge of how Artificial Intelligences behave in this new era of semi-sentient AIs)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> How should cyberware gadgets work? I'm guessing that you could make a list of them and then buy them as Merits.<br /> <br /> Now the tricky part is Character Creation particularly when it comes to fully cyberized characters.<br /> What about the difference between Full Body Cyborgs like Batou &amp; Kusanagi VS partially cyberized humans? FBC should at least have Physical Attributes like an above-average human ( 3 dots) and in several cases they're superhuman in this regard. So how to handle that? Should they begin with more free dots in Physical? Should they have more dots to spend overall (like 8/6/4 from Ex3)? If attributes go beyond 5 does it break the system?<br /> <br /> Alternatively should I change character creation towards selecting a particular body model as a package of Merits &amp; Physical Attributes and then give some dots to spend on other Merits and Skills?<br /> <br /> Other stuff I've been musing is to include Stunting rules (like in Exalted) for a more over the top cinematic feeling. And maybe change how damage works in robots/androids/cyborgs?<br /> Possibly include a &quot;Strain&quot; track that you fill up when you spend willpower to add dice (more like Solar Excellencies) in order to succeed to truly superhuman tasks (like how Kusanagi tries to open the tank's hatch and breaks off her two arms in the process)<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway, there are many stuff in my head but I'm a Storyteller/Storytelling newbie so I don't think I can pull it off without any advice.<br /> <br /> So, if you are interested in helping out or if you know any such conversions feel free to comment below <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT: I know about Bleeding Edge but it doesn't have anything of real use to me<br /> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\">\u039a\u03c1\u03ac\u03c4\u03b1 \u03c4\u03bf</span></div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2671,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2671-legopaidi","user":"legopaidi","date":". 08-31-2016, 06:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2671-legopaidi","name":"legopaidi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T06:48:10-07:00","id":961021,"title":"","content":"I tired, but I had a better time using shadowrun","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T07:50:52-07:00","id":961054,"title":"","content":"FATE sounds like another good alternate system.<br /> <br /> But speaking of CofD, Deviant sounds like it is pretty much intended towards such systems. Hurt Lock also has a &quot;micro template&quot; (the Lost Boys) who use a set of &quot;Supernatural&quot; Merits to simulate cyberware. Depending on how far you wish to go, I'd look there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T10:34:22-07:00","id":961110,"title":"","content":"I tried doing it with Fate and I while I like the system it didn't feel right to me.It's much more metagamey than I would like a GITS campaign to be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2671-legopaidi","name":"legopaidi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T10:21:34-07:00","id":961755,"title":"","content":"I would take a look at Demon the Descent...there's a whole thing in the ST guide about an alternate cyberpunk city. And it would be pretty easy to map demon's cover system into one representing hackers taking on the authorities. Hunter the Vigil's Task force Valkerie, Network Zero, and Chieron Group all have merits that could be modeled into a post-human setting.<br /> <br /> Also World of Darkness Mirrors has a whole section about skill tricks that would make a game much more cinematic. World of Darkness: Demon Hunter X has a group of Japanese cyborg (boy that word sounds dated) monster hunters, the M20 and Iteration X have magical versions of this stuff (in fact nearly all of the new Technocracy Convention books are excellent for ideas about how to use cutting edge or sci-fi elements in WoD/CofD).<br /> <br /> Last but not least, whenever Trinity Continuum comes out you'll probably get a full set of gear you can convert over to CofD.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1783-spanishinquisition","name":"SpanishInquisition","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1783_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}